# Virtual Space — local development settings. Copy to .env and edit.
# Everything here has a safe default; nothing here is a secret.

# --- identity -------------------------------------------------------------
# Behind IAP in the cloud (TRUST_IAP_HEADER=1); unset locally, so a dev
# identity stands in and ?as=someone@local picks who you are.
# TRUST_IAP_HEADER=1
# IAP_JWT_AUDIENCE=/projects/<number>/locations/<region>/services/<service>

# Who you are locally when ?as= is not given. This address is also the local
# admin by default, which means it has NO avatar — it is the TA.
# DEV_USER=jade@local

# Instructor allowlist. An admin IS the TA and has no student avatar, so
# adding an address here removes that person from the world as a student.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=someone@gmail.com

# --- the class roster -----------------------------------------------------
# Which student character each address controls. Slots: s1 (Sam), s2 (Ben),
# s3 (Chloe), s4 (Dev), s5 (Grace), jade. A slot with an address assigned has
# no AI stand-in — that office belongs to a person. An address with no slot
# still gets in, but spawns in the Common Area and is logged at join.
# STUDENTS=someone@gmail.com=jade,student1@example.com=s1

# Display names, overriding the character's placeholder name. Use this once
# you know what a student is actually called.
# ROSTER=student1@example.com:Alex Rivera

# --- idle behaviour -------------------------------------------------------
# The TA office holds one student; these free it when they go quiet.
# SOLO_WARN_S=240
# SOLO_IDLE_S=300
# Anywhere else: no operation at all for this long and a student is walked
# back to their own office.
# HOME_IDLE_S=600

# --- LLM ------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
# OLLAMA_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=            # keep in .env, never commit

# --- persistence ----------------------------------------------------------
# SNAPSHOT_URI=gs://your-bucket/state
